            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F004\", \"F006\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"In subsection (e)(2), the introductory text specifies 'the employee—' as the actor who 'shall provide the employer with not less than 30 days’ notice' under subparagraph (B). The draft incorrectly assigned 'the employer' as the actor. Correcting the actor and actor_quote to 'the employee' is a necessary correction that faithfully reflects the source text.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F004\", \"F006\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Under subsection (e)(2)(B), the duty to provide notice is imposed on the employee, not the health care provider. Designating 'the health care provider' as the actor is contradicted by the source text.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0002\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F004\", \"F006\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The exception in subsection (e)(2)(B) ('except that if the date of the treatment requires leave to begin in less than 30 days, the employee shall provide such notice as is practicable') directly qualifies the general 30-day advance notice requirement in subparagraph (B), which is represented by claim C0002. Setting relation to 'exception' and qualifying C0002 correctly links the exception to its governing requirement.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0003\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F004\", \"F005\", \"F006\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The exception in subsection (e)(2)(B) relaxes the 30-day notice requirement for medical treatment leave, not the scheduling duty under subsection (e)(2)(A) represented by claim C0001. Linking the exception to C0001 is incorrect.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
